{"nodes":[{"id":"9f26f662240e01fd","type":"text","text":"Recurrent\n\n循环的","x":50,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120},{"id":"bccfdc96d9631503","type":"text","text":"convolutional\n\n卷积","x":330,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"443796679c7c1f77","type":"text","text":"self-respect\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: A feeling of pride and confidence in oneself; a sense of one’s own worth or value.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 自尊  \n4) **Example sentence**: Most of us strive for self-respect — to see ourselves in a positive light, to be proud of who we are.","x":610,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"85ac05e21491746c","type":"text","text":"undermine\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Verb  \n2) **English definition**: To weaken or damage something, especially someone’s confidence, authority, or feelings, often gradually or insidiously.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 削弱；损害；暗中破坏  \n4) **Example sentence**: Any comments or experiences that undermine those feelings of self-worth can be uncomfortable.","x":50,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"45aa5cd8bc91fc10","type":"text","text":"perception\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: The way in which something is regarded, understood, or interpreted, often based on sensory experience or mental awareness.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 感知；认知；看法  \n4) **Example sentence**: \"Perception D.\" (The original sentence is incomplete, but a full example: \"Her perception of the situation changed after learning the truth.\")","x":330,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"49a5cc4526688794","type":"text","text":"citation\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: A reference to a source (such as a book, article, or legal case) that provides authority or evidence for a statement or claim.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 引用；引证  \n4) **Example sentence**: *Citation B* refers to the second source listed in the bibliography.","x":610,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"b6859ac9f45b5928","type":"text","text":"imitation\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: The act of copying or reproducing something, often as a less authentic or inferior version.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 模仿；仿制品  \n4) **Example sentence**: *imitation C.* (This suggests \"imitation\" is used as a label or category, likely meaning a copy or replica of type C.)","x":50,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"085b47fec20196fe","type":"text","text":"foolish\n\n1) Part of speech: Adjective  \n2) English definition: Lacking good sense, judgment, or wisdom; unwise.  \n3) Chinese translation: 愚蠢的；不明智的  \n4) Example sentence: It was foolish of him to go out in the rain without an umbrella.","x":330,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"fc06e4b1b1ab9ca7","type":"text","text":"interpreting\n\n1) **Part of speech:** Verb (gerund/present participle)  \n2) **Chinese translation:** 解读 / 诠释  \n3) **Example sentence:** She kept interpreting his silence as a sign of disapproval.","x":610,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"8966ac0e444ac23b","type":"text","text":"term\n\n1) Part of speech: noun  \n2) Chinese translation: 术语；说法  \n3) Example sentence: The term for this way of thinking is personalisation.","x":50,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"d6094b883bfc9411","type":"text","text":"quotations\n\nBased on the context provided (the fragment \"quotations B\"), here is the definition:\n\n1) **Part of speech:** Noun (plural)\n2) **Chinese translation:** 引用/报价 (bàojià) — specifically referring to price quotes or estimates in a business or financial context.\n3) **Example sentence:** \"Please send us your latest quotations for product B.\"","x":330,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"ce70f6230dd761f2","type":"text","x":610,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"at work\n\n短语，起作用","color":"2"},{"id":"d0c17ed99dd591f4","type":"text","x":50,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"accounting for\n\nBased on the context provided (which appears to be a fragment, likely from a sentence like \"X is responsible for accounting for C\"), here is the definition:\n\n1)  **Part of speech:** Phrasal verb (prepositional verb)\n2)  **Detailed Chinese translation:** 解释；说明；占（比例）；对…负责\n3)  **Example sentence for each meaning:**\n    *   **Meaning 1 (To explain or give a reason):** The manager had to **account for** the missing funds. (经理必须**解释**资金丢失的原因。)\n    *   **Meaning 2 (To constitute a specified portion):** The service sector **accounts for** over 60% of the country's GDP. (服务业**占**该国GDP的60%以上。)\n    *   **Meaning 3 (To be responsible for):** Each employee is **accounting for** their own time sheet. (每位员工都要**对**自己的考勤表**负责**。)","color":"2"},{"id":"213bb1a50c576684","type":"text","x":330,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"interfering with\n\nBased on the context provided (only the phrase \"interfering with\"), here is the definition:\n\n1)  **Part of speech:** Verb phrase (present participle of \"interfere with\")\n2)  **Detailed Chinese translation:** 干涉；妨碍；干扰；介入（并阻碍）\n3)  **Example sentence for each meaning:**\n    *   **干涉 (to meddle):** Stop **interfering with** my personal life.\n    *   **妨碍 (to hinder/obstruct):** The storm is **interfering with** our travel plans.\n    *   **干扰 (to disrupt):** Please don't **interfere with** the machine while it's running.","color":"1"}],"edges":[]}